class=\"px-2 pb-2 text-[11px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-400\">Calculators</div><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2\"><a class=\"rounded-lg bg-slate-900 px-4 py-3.5 text-center text-sm font-black text-white hover:bg-slate-800 transition-colors\" href=\"/#calculator-workspace\">LCA Calculator</a><a class=\"rounded-lg bg-emerald-600 px-4 py-3.5 text-center text-sm font-black text-white hover:bg-emerald-500 transition-colors\" href=\"/cbam-calculator\">CBAM Calculator</a></div></div><a class=\"mt-2 rounded-lg px-3 py-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700 hover:bg-emerald-50\" href=\"/\">The Engine</a><a class=\"rounded-lg px-3 py-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700 hover:bg-emerald-50\" href=\"/cbam-calculator\">CBAM Calculator</a><a class=\"rounded-lg px-3 py-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700 hover:bg-emerald-50\" href=\"/guides\">LCA Guides</a><a class=\"rounded-lg px-3 py-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700 hover:bg-emerald-50\" href=\"/methodology\">Methodology</a><div class=\"mt-2 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 p-3\"><div class=\"px-2 pb-2 text-[11px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-400\">Popular learning guides</div><a class=\"block rounded-lg px-2 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-600 hover:text-emerald-700 hover:bg-white\" href=\"/embodied-carbon-calculator\">Embodied Carbon Calculator Guide</a><a class=\"block rounded-lg px-2 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-600 hover:text-emerald-700 hover:bg-white\" href=\"/a1-a3-embodied-carbon\">A1-A3 Embodied Carbon</a><a class=\"block rounded-lg px-2 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-600 hover:text-emerald-700 hover:bg-white\" href=\"/epd-carbon-calculator\">EPD Carbon Calculator</a><a class=\"block rounded-lg px-2 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-600 hover:text-emerald-700 hover:bg-white\" href=\"/whole-building-lca\">Whole-Building LCA</a></div><a class=\"mt-2 rounded-lg px-3 py-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700 hover:bg-emerald-50\" href=\"/about\">About Us</a><a class=\"rounded-lg px-3 py-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700 hover:bg-emerald-50\" href=\"/contact\">Contact</a></div><div class=\"pt-5 mt-4 border-t border-slate-200\"><a class=\"block text-center bg-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-800 text-white px-5 py-4 rounded-lg text-base font-bold shadow-md transition-all\" href=\"/#calculator-workspace\">Launch LCA Workspace</a></div></div></div></details></div></div></nav></header><div class=\"flex-1\"><main class=\"min-h-screen bg-slate-50\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"TechArticle\",\"headline\":\"Building LCA Methodology: Embodied Carbon A1-D\",\"description\":\"A transparent building LCA methodology for quantities, EPD units, A1-A3, A4, B4 replacements, C1-C4, Module D, baseline comparison and data quality.\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-08-31\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":\"https://greenengineeringtools.com/methodology\",\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Green Engineering Tools\",\"url\":\"https://greenengineeringtools.com\"},\"about\":[\"Life cycle assessment\",\"Embodied carbon\",\"Environmental Product Declarations\",\"Building materials\"]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://greenengineeringtools.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Guides\",\"item\":\"https://greenengineeringtools.com/guides\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Building LCA Methodology: Embodied Carbon A1-D\",\"item\":\"https://greenengineeringtools.com/methodology\"}]}</script><section class=\"bg-slate-950 text-white\"><div class=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-14 sm:py-20\"><nav class=\"text-sm text-slate-400 mb-7\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><a class=\"hover:text-white\" href=\"/\">Home</a><span class=\"mx-2\">/</span><a class=\"hover:text-white\" href=\"/guides\">Guides</a></nav><p class=\"text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-emerald-300\">Calculation methodology</p><h1 class=\"mt-4 max-w-5xl text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-black tracking-tight\">Building LCA Methodology: Embodied Carbon A1-D</h1><p class=\"mt-6 max-w-4xl text-lg sm:text-xl leading-8 text-slate-300\">A transparent building LCA methodology for quantities, EPD units, A1-A3, A4, B4 replacements, C1-C4, Module D, baseline comparison and data quality.</p><div class=\"mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-emerald-500 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-black text-white hover:bg-emerald-400\" href=\"/#calculator-workspace\">Open the LCA calculator</a><a class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-900 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-800\" href=\"/methodology\">Read methodology</a></div><p class=\"mt-6 text-xs text-slate-500\">Last reviewed: <!-- -->2026-08-31</p></div></section><div class=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 grid lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_280px] gap-10\"><article class=\"min-w-0\"><div class=\"space-y-14\"><section id=\"purpose\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\">What this LCA methodology is designed to do</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">The Green Engineering Tools calculation methodology is designed to turn project material quantities into transparent lifecycle results without hiding the assumptions that materially affect the answer. A quantity is only useful when it is tied to a unit, a material or EPD dataset, a declared quantity, a lifecycle boundary and a study period. The engine therefore treats material resolution and unit compatibility as part of the calculation rather than as an administrative step.</p><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">The methodology is intended for design studies, embodied-carbon screening, EPD-based comparisons, baseline-versus-proposed analysis and structured reporting. It is not a substitute for professional judgment or a certification decision. Formal reports should be reviewed against the standard, rating system and project-specific requirements that apply to the work.</p></section><section id=\"data-hierarchy\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\">Data hierarchy: prefer traceable datasets over convenient guesses</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">A professional LCA workflow should make the source of each environmental factor visible. Product-specific EPD data can be valuable when the product, geography, declared unit and scope are appropriate. Industry-average or generic datasets can still be useful in early design, but they should be identified as such so users understand the level of specificity behind the result.</p><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">The calculator intentionally treats an unmapped material as unresolved. It does not create a default manufacturing value, default end-of-life value or fabricated impact category merely to complete the total. That behavior is important because a visually complete result can be more misleading than an explicit data gap.</p><ul class=\"mt-5 space-y-3 list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700 leading-7\"><li>Keep the dataset ID or source reference with the calculated material.</li><li>Preserve the manufacturer, declared unit, declared quantity and available lifecycle modules.</li><li>Keep missing environmental indicators unavailable rather than changing them to zero.</li><li>Retain the original BIM or CSV material alias even when the engineer searches EC3 using a corrected or simplified name.</li></ul></section><section id=\"units\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\">Quantity normalization and declared units</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">Environmental Product Declarations report impacts against a declared or functional quantity. A project schedule may use kilograms, tonnes, cubic metres, square metres, linear metres or pieces. Before multiplying quantity by an EPD factor, the project quantity must be converted to the basis used by the dataset.</p><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">Straight conversions such as kilograms to tonnes or square feet to square metres can be handled directly. Cross-dimensional conversions need physical information. Converting mass to volume requires density; converting area to volume requires thickness. When the required conversion data is missing, the safer response is to flag the row instead of inventing a density or thickness.</p></section><section id=\"modules\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\">Lifecycle modules A1-D</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">The engine stores lifecycle information by module rather than collapsing the entire building into four generic phases. This keeps the result auditable and makes it possible to distinguish product-stage impacts from transportation, replacement and end-of-life scenarios.</p><div class=\"mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white\"><table class=\"w-full min-w-[640px] text-sm\"><thead class=\"bg-slate-900 text-white\"><tr><th class=\"p-3 text-left font-black\">Module</th><th class=\"p-3 text-left font-black\">Typical meaning</th><th class=\"p-3 text-left font-black\">Treatment in the engine</th></tr></thead><tbody class=\"divide-y divide-slate-200\"><tr class=\"align-top\"><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">A1-A3</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Raw material supply, transport associated with production, and manufacturing</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Uses declared product-stage impacts from the selected dataset.</td></tr><tr class=\"align-top\"><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">A4</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Transport from production or supply location to the project site</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Can be calculated from product mass, transport mode and distance when project-specific data is available.</td></tr><tr class=\"align-top\"><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">A5</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Construction and installation</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Kept separate from manufacturing and transport.</td></tr><tr class=\"align-top\"><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">B1-B3</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Use, maintenance and repair</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Included only when the selected methodology and dataset provide applicable values.</td></tr><tr class=\"align-top\"><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">B4</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Replacement</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Triggered by service-life assumptions during the building study period rather than multiplying the initial A-stage total.</td></tr><tr class=\"align-top\"><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">B5-B7</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Refurbishment, operational energy and operational water</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Tracked separately; operational energy should not be multiplied across every material row.</td></tr><tr class=\"align-top\"><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">C1-C4</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Deconstruction, transport, waste processing and disposal</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Reported as end-of-life impacts when the required scenario or dataset is available.</td></tr><tr class=\"align-top\"><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">D</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Benefits and loads beyond the system boundary</td><td class=\"p-3 leading-6 text-slate-700\">Shown separately from A-C and never replaced with a generic recycling credit.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section id=\"transport\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\">A4 transport calculations</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">A4 represents transportation of construction products to the project site. A practical project-specific calculation needs the mass being moved, the travel distance and the transport mode. Building Transparency describes the same core inputs for EC3 A4 calculations: product weight, transportation mode and transportation distance.</p><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">When a project quantity is not expressed by mass, the calculation needs mass per declared unit or another defensible way to determine mass. A transport result should be flagged when mass is unknown rather than assuming that every material unit weighs the same amount.</p><div class=\"mt-6 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5\"><h3 class=\"font-black text-amber-950\">Do not confuse A4 with A1-A3</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-amber-900\">A product EPD&#x27;s manufacturing GWP and project delivery emissions are different lifecycle contributions. Keeping them separate makes design and procurement decisions easier to explain.</p></div></section><section id=\"replacement\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\">Replacement and study period logic</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">A building study period may be longer than the reference service life of finishes, insulation, membranes or other products. When replacement is required, the replacement event belongs in the use stage, commonly B4. The methodology therefore separates the initial product from later replacement events instead of simply multiplying A1-A5 by a rounded replacement count.</p><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">Service-life assumptions can materially change whole-life results. Baseline and proposed comparisons should use consistent study periods, and service lives should be documented so reviewers can reproduce the scenario.</p></section><section id=\"end-of-life\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\">C1-C4 and Module D are not the same thing</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">End-of-life processing still causes impacts even when a material is recyclable. Demolition, transport, sorting, processing and residual disposal should not disappear merely because the recovery percentage reaches 100 percent.</p><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">Module D is a separate accounting of potential benefits or loads beyond the assessed system boundary. The engine therefore keeps Module D outside the A-C result and only reports it when the source dataset or an explicitly documented scenario supports it.</p></section><section id=\"comparison\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\">Baseline and proposed building comparisons</h2><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">A meaningful comparison requires more than two uploaded spreadsheets. The models should represent functionally comparable buildings or options, use the same study period and apply consistent software, datasets and boundaries. Large differences in floor area, building function or omitted systems can overwhelm the effect of a material substitution.</p><p class=\"mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-8 text-slate-700\">For certification-oriented work, use the exact equivalence rules of the applicable rating system. The calculator&#x27;s comparison interface supports design analysis, but certification decisions remain the responsibility of the project team and reviewing authority.</p></section><section id=\"quality\" class=\"scroll-mt-24\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950\">Data quality checks before trusting the total</h2><ul class=\"mt-5 space-y-3 list-disc pl-6 text-slate-700 leading-7\"><li>Resolve unmapped materials or quantify how much of the project remains unmapped.</li><li>Review unit-conversion warnings and verify density or thickness assumptions.</li><li>Confirm which lifecycle modules are declared and which are not declared.</li><li>Check service-life assumptions for products that may be replaced.</li><li>Confirm A4 transport mode and distance when transportation is material to the result.</li><li>Keep Module D separate from the A-C result.</li><li>Export the same calculation core to the dashboard, CSV and PDF so totals do not diverge.</li></ul><div class=\"mt-6 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5\"><h3 class=\"font-black text-amber-950\">ND does not mean zero</h3><p class=\"mt-2 leading-7 text-amber-900\">If an EPD does not declare a module or indicator, treating the missing result as zero can materially understate impact. The calculation should preserve the absence of data.</p></div></section></div><section class=\"mt-16 border-t border-slate-200 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-950\">Frequently asked questions</h2><div class=\"mt-6 space-y-3\"><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white\"><summary class=\"cursor-pointer list-none p-5 font-black text-slate-900 flex gap-4 justify-between\"><span>What is an embodied carbon calculation methodology?</span><span class=\"text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform\">+</span></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-slate-700 leading-7\">It is the documented set of rules used to convert material quantities and environmental datasets into lifecycle results. A good methodology states the system boundary, units, study period, data sources, transport and replacement assumptions, end-of-life treatment, and how missing data is handled.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white\"><summary class=\"cursor-pointer list-none p-5 font-black text-slate-900 flex gap-4 justify-between\"><span>Why does the calculator refuse to guess a value for an unknown material?</span><span class=\"text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform\">+</span></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-slate-700 leading-7\">A default number can make an incomplete model look precise. The tool flags unknown materials so the user can map them to a defensible dataset or explicitly document a proxy.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white\"><summary class=\"cursor-pointer list-none p-5 font-black text-slate-900 flex gap-4 justify-between\"><span>Is Module D subtracted from the whole-building A-C result?</span><span class=\"text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform\">+</span></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-slate-700 leading-7\">No. Module D represents benefits or loads beyond the system boundary and should be reported separately unless a particular reporting framework explicitly instructs otherwise.</div></details><details class=\"group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white\"><summary class=\"cursor-pointer list-none p-5 font-black text-slate-900 flex gap-4 justify-between\"><span>Can the same methodology be used for every certification system?</span><span class=\"text-emerald-600 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform\">+</span></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-slate-700 leading-7\">No. The calculation core can support multiple frameworks, but each rating system may define different scope, equivalence, impact categories, service periods or reporting rules.</div></details></div></section><section class=\"mt-14 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-slate-950\">Authoritative references</h2><p class=\"mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600\">These links are provided for readers who want to verify standards, product data terminology, or certification requirements at the source.</p><ul class=\"mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm\"><li><a href=\"https://docs.buildingtransparency.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"font-bold text-blue-700 hover:underline\">Building Transparency documentation — EC3 and tallyLCA scope</a></li><li><a href=\"https://docs.buildingtransparency.org/ec3/main-features/plan-and-compare-buildings/a4-transportation-emissions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"font-bold text-blue-700 hover:underline\">Building Transparency — A4 transportation emissions</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.usgbc.org/node/2755842\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"font-bold text-blue-700 hover:underline\">USGBC — LEED v4 Building Life-Cycle Impact Reduction guide</a></li></ul></section><section class=\"mt-14\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-black text-slate-950\">Continue learning</h2><div class=\"mt-5 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4\"><a class=\"rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:shadow-sm transition\" href=\"/embodied-carbon-calculator\"><h3 class=\"font-black text-slate-950\">Embodied carbon calculator guide</h3><p class=\"mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600\">Learn how to turn a construction material schedule into an auditable carbon result.</p></a><a class=\"rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:shadow-sm transition\" href=\"/epd-carbon-calculator\"><h3 class=\"font-black text-slate-950\">EPD carbon calculator</h3><p class=\"mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600\">Learn how to read EPD units, GWP values, declared modules and data limitations.</p></a><a class=\"rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:shadow-sm transition\" href=\"/whole-building-lca\"><h3 class=\"font-black text-slate-950\">Whole-building LCA guide</h3><p class=\"mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600\">Understand scope, service life, baseline comparison and whole-life reporting.</p></a><a class=\"rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:shadow-sm transition\" href=\"/module-d-lca\"><h3 class=\"font-black text-slate-950\">Module D explained</h3><p class=\"mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600\">Understand recycling and reuse benefits beyond the system boundary without double counting.</p></a></div></section></article><aside class=\"hidden lg:block\"><div class=\"sticky top-24 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5\"><h2 class=\"text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-500\">On this page</h2><nav class=\"mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm\"><a href=\"#purpose\" class=\"block font-semibold leading-5 text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700\">What this LCA methodology is designed to do</a><a href=\"#data-hierarchy\" class=\"block font-semibold leading-5 text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700\">Data hierarchy: prefer traceable datasets over convenient guesses</a><a href=\"#units\" class=\"block font-semibold leading-5 text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700\">Quantity normalization and declared units</a><a href=\"#modules\" class=\"block font-semibold leading-5 text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700\">Lifecycle modules A1-D</a><a href=\"#transport\" class=\"block font-semibold leading-5 text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700\">A4 transport calculations</a><a href=\"#replacement\" class=\"block font-semibold leading-5 text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700\">Replacement and study period logic</a><a href=\"#end-of-life\" class=\"block font-semibold leading-5 text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700\">C1-C4 and Module D are not the same thing</a><a href=\"#comparison\" class=\"block font-semibold leading-5 text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700\">Baseline and proposed building comparisons</a><a href=\"#quality\" class=\"block font-semibold leading-5 text-slate-700 hover:text-emerald-700\">Data quality checks before trusting the total</a><a href=\"#top\" class=\"block pt-3 border-t border-slate-100 font-bold text-slate-400 hover:text-slate-700\">Back to top</a></nav></div></aside></div></main><!--$--><!--/$--></div><footer class=\"bg-slate-950 text-slate-400 border-t border-slate-800 w-full mt-auto\"><div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-14\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-9 lg:gap-8\"><div class=\"sm:col-span-2 lg:col-span-1\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center\" href=\"/\"><svg class=\"w-7 h-7 text-emerald-500 mr-2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" d=\"M19 21V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v16m14 0h2m-2 0h-5m-9 0H3m2 0h5M9 7h1m-1 4h1m4-4h1m-1 4h1m-5 10v-5a1 1 0 011-1h2a1 1 0 011 1v5m-4 0h4\"></path></svg><span class=\"font-black text-white tracking-tight\">GreenEngineering Tools</span></a><p class=\"mt-4 max-w-xs text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400\">Browser-based tools and practical guides for embodied carbon, EPD data, BIM material workflows and whole-building life-cycle assessment.</p><a class=\"mt-5 inline-flex text-sm font-black text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300\" href=\"/#calculator-workspace\">Open LCA calculator →</a></div><div><h2 class=\"text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-white\">Tools</h2><nav class=\"mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm\" aria-label=\"Footer tools navigation\"><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/\">LCA Engine</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/cbam-calculator\">CBAM Estimator</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/methodology\">Methodology</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/guides\">All Guides</a></nav></div><div class=\"sm:col-span-2 lg:col-span-1\"><h2 class=\"text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-white\">Learn</h2><nav class=\"mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm\" aria-label=\"Footer learning navigation\"><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/embodied-carbon-calculator\">Embodied Carbon Calculator</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/a1-a3-embodied-carbon\">A1-A3 Embodied Carbon</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/epd-carbon-calculator\">EPD Carbon Calculator</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/ec3-epd-guide\">EC3 EPD Guide</a></nav></div><div><h2 class=\"text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-white\">More Guides</h2><nav class=\"mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm\" aria-label=\"Footer additional guides\"><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/bim-embodied-carbon\">BIM Embodied Carbon</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/whole-building-lca\">Whole-Building LCA</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/module-d-lca\">Module D Explained</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/leed-whole-building-lca\">LEED Whole-Building LCA</a></nav></div><div><h2 class=\"text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-white\">Company</h2><nav class=\"mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm\" aria-label=\"Footer company navigation\"><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/about\">About Us</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/contact\">Contact</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/privacy-policy\">Privacy Policy</a><a class=\"block hover:text-white transition-colors\" href=\"/terms\">Terms</a></nav></div></div><div class=\"mt-10 pt-7 border-t border-slate-800 flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 justif